# ==============================================================================
# GEMINI_API_KEY CONFIGURATION & BUILDCONFIG VERIFICATION GUIDE
# ==============================================================================
# 
# STEP 1: OBTAIN GEMINI API KEY
# -----------------------------
# Generate a valid Gemini API Key from Google AI Studio:
# https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
#
# STEP 2: CONFIGURE IN SECRETS PANEL
# -----------------------------------
# 1. Open the "Secrets" panel on the left sidebar of Google AI Studio.
# 2. Add a new secret entry:
#    - Secret Key: GEMINI_API_KEY
#    - Secret Value: <YOUR_GENERATED_API_KEY>
# 3. Save the secret.
#
# STEP 3: VERIFY BUILDCONFIG INJECTION DURING BUILD
# -------------------------------------------------
# When Gradle builds the Android app, the Secrets Gradle Plugin reads
# GEMINI_API_KEY from environment secrets and generates:
#
#   com.example.BuildConfig.GEMINI_API_KEY
#
# You can verify key status directly inside the application:
# 1. Open the "Aegis AI Co-Pilot" screen or "Governance" screen.
# 2. Check the top diagnostic banner (`AegisAiStatusView`).
# 3. If connected, it will display "LIVE GEMINI AI CONNECTED".
# 4. If missing or placeholder ("MY_GEMINI_API_KEY"), the app automatically
#    activates "Fail-Safe Mode (Local Security Simulation)" without crashing.
#
# ==============================================================================

GEMINI_API_KEY=MY_GEMINI_API_KEY


